      {
        "comment_id": "2922105603",
        "repo_full_name": "Azure/azure-powershell",
        "pr_number": 29111,
        "pr_file": "src/Functions/Functions.Autorest/custom/Update-AzFunctionApp.ps1",
        "discussion_id": "2922105603",
        "commented_code": null,
        "comment_created_at": "2026-03-12T03:48:12+00:00",
        "comment_author": "Francisco-Gamino",
        "comment_body": " This should be `[System.Management.Automation.SwitchParameter]`, not `[System.Boolean]`.\n\n- New-AzFunctionApp.ps1 (line 177) already uses SwitchParameter for the same parameter \u2014 these must match.\n- [bool] is a PowerShell anti-pattern \u2014 the -Enable* naming convention implies a flag. Boolean forces awkward syntax like -EnableSystemAssignedIdentity $true.\n- SwitchParameter handles all three states \u2014 enable (presence), disable (:$false), don't touch (omit). The existing logic at lines 175\u2013210 uses $PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey() and -eq $true/$false, which work identically with Switch. No logic changes needed.\n- The test already uses switch syntax \u2014 New-Update-Remove-AzFunctionApp.Tests.ps1:246 uses -EnableSystemAssignedIdentity:$false.\n- A separate -DisableSystemAssignedIdentity is not needed \u2014 it would create mutual-exclusion complexity, break consistency with New-AzFunctionApp, and go against Azure PowerShell precedent (e.g., Set-AzKeyVault -EnablePurgeProtection has no -Disable counterpart).\n\nCascading fixes needed in help/Update-AzFunctionApp.md: syntax (lines 19, 26), examples (lines 45, 59), and parameter type (lines 125\u2013136).",
        "pr_file_module": null
      }
    ]
  },
